  "summary": {
    "ideas": [
      "When $x$ is on both sides, take the same amount of $x$ from each side. That collects it on one side.",
      "Collect on the side with more $x$, and the $x$ term stays positive.",
      "If the $x$ terms cancel, a false line such as $7 = 3$ means no solution; a true line means every $x$ works."
    ],
    "formula": {
      "name": "Collecting the unknown",
      "tex": "ax + b = cx + d \\;\\Rightarrow\\; (a - c)x = d - b \\;\\Rightarrow\\; x = \\dfrac{d - b}{a - c}",
      "note": "Needs $a \\neq c$. When $a = c$ there is no solution, or every $x$ works."
    },
    "trap": "Taking $2x$ off the right means taking it off the left too: $7x + 3 = 2x + 18$ becomes $5x + 3 = 18$, not $9x + 3 = 18$."
  },
